T071 design context: the playtest picked leading over shortening the flight or widening the tolerance because both alternatives tax every throw (a sub-1 s flight breaks the readable section-14 arc for stationary targets too, and a fatter contact or standard splash wakes sleepers the player did not choose — the pre-fix probes already showed wrong-walker wakes). The lead reads velocity at throw time and scales by flight_time_seconds, so the assist stays honest wherever the flight value is tuned later; the range clamp keeps the 500 px throw rule meaningful against outbound chasers. dodge_cooldown_seconds counts from roll start (0.8 s vs the 0.4 s roll) so the uptime ceiling is duration/cooldown regardless of frame jitter; it is a prototype value for Niko's hands-on pass. Mash values were left alone on probe evidence: every cadence from 0.12 s to 0.5 s per press breaks the hug inside 2 s at a 7-30 meter cost, far from the ~6.7 s a hug needs to empty a full meter, so slow tapping punishes without killing. Probe logs live in the task artifact dir (t071-*-probe-*.log); the probe scripts were temporary and deleted.
